Closed form expressions are proposed for the Feynman integral
  $$
  I_{D, m}(p,q) = \int\frac{d^my}{(2π)^m}\int\frac{d^Dx}{(2π)^D}
  \frac1{(x-p/2)^2+(y-q/2)^4}
  \frac1{(x+p/2)^2+(y+q/2)^4}
  $$ over $d=D+m$ dimensional space with $(x,y),\,(p,q)\in \mathbb R^D \oplus \mathbb R^m$, in the special case $D=1$. We show that $I_{1,m}(p,q)$ can be expressed in different forms involving real and imaginary parts of the complex variable Gauss hypergeometric function $_2F_1$, as well as generalized hype
